{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EJnsqsJtkXYuK5EpKrdZTu","type":"tool_result","content":"969:Briefly, because you'll see all of this again: requests are the input to the scheduler's filtering step *[cross-bearing: see Ch 7 §2 — resource requests as a scheduling filter]*. They're what the system is reporting on when a Pod is killed for using too much *[cross-bearing: see Ch 13 §4 — OOMKilled and Evicted]*. They're the baseline autoscalers compare observed usage against *[cross-bearing: see Ch 17 — autoscaling targets]*, and they're the denominator when monitoring reports \"utilization\" *[cross-bearing: see Ch 18 §3 — utilization relative to requests]*.\n1027:This item required §5 and §8 together, which is the point: it's the direct precursor to Chapter 13's material on diagnosing killed and evicted Pods. What we're **not** doing here is diagnosing it. Naming the mechanism is this chapter's job. Which command to run and which events to read is Chapter 13's *[cross-bearing: see Ch 13 §4 — OOMKilled and Evicted]*.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"97701b12-b3c3-4cfe-8e09-ff21e20634b5","uuid":"6e8c048b-8926-4654-8aa5-f547e49bea9e","timestamp":"2026-08-24T19:57:53.074Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"969:Briefly, because you'll see all of this again: requests are the input to the scheduler's filtering step *[cross-bearing: see Ch 7 §2 — resource requests as a scheduling filter]*. They're what the system is reporting on when a Pod is killed for using too much *[cross-bearing: see Ch 13 §4 — OOMKilled and Evicted]*. They're the baseline autoscalers compare observed usage against *[cross-bearing: see Ch 17 — autoscaling targets]*, and they're the denominator when monitoring reports \"utilization\" *[cross-bearing: see Ch 18 §3 — utilization relative to requests]*.\n1027:This item required §5 and §8 together, which is the point: it's the direct precursor to Chapter 13's material on diagnosing killed and evicted Pods. What we're **not** doing here is diagnosing it. Naming the mechanism is this chapter's job. Which command to run and which events to read is Chapter 13's *[cross-bearing: see Ch 13 §4 — OOMKilled and Evicted]*.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
